                        



SCP-4273 is an island just off the coast of Greenland, very much resembling the shape of the island from the beloved children’s book series, “The Railway Series”. It appears to be a fully functioning society, though, no human entities inhabit the island.

Though no humans inhabit the island, all machinery, vehicles, and houses remain, all resembling that of an early 20th century civilization.

Reports of the island and it’s anomalous features date back to 4/20/1998, when some fishermen rowed their boat out to the island, after some sudden gurgling noises as if one of the fishermen had fallen overboard, one man jumped ship and discovered a facial-esque growth on the front of the boat. No traces of organs or any human body parts were found, even after cutting the boat up on the Island’s ground.

All instances of these living objects are to be classified as SCP-4273-1.

Test 1: A stone

Details: D-9341 was instructed to pick up a rock and throw it into the water, however the moment D-9341 picked up the rock it became sentient and instantly had a face grow on a flat surface of the rock.

Test 2: A Bus

Details: Researcher █████████ was told to drive a bus from one end of the parking lot to the other. The moment that Researcher █████████ turned the key the bus became sentient, and started talking about how nobody had been there in ages. After the bus was shut off it took 30 minutes for the face to disappear.

                    

                                    





            
    

                    



                    
                        
                            
